Scribo is an easy to learn, exciting and challenging puzzle game with its roots in crossword puzzles.

However, unlike a traditional crossword, Scribo has only ten interlocking words, each of five letters.

Because the words interlock the words are the clues, but to get you started, two letters are already placed on the board.

There are thirty letters in the picker, twenty five for the ten words and an extra word to add a little spice.

Each letter has a value which adds up to give each word a score.

As you place letters on the board making words, they are popped into the found words bag and contribute to your final score.

When you find a legal word, it is highlit on the board in yellow.

When you find a word which belongs on the board, it is highlit in orange, and if it is in the right place, it is highlit in green.